  "body": "The spec at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/timers-and-user-prompts.html#printing seems to disregard the long-established practice by many browsers of blocking `window.print()` while the print dialog is open. Will there be any attempt to write the specification such that it matches both behaviors seen in the wild? (E.g. Chrome and Firefox still block, Safari used to but does no longer, apparently IE maybe [sort of](https://stackoverflow.com/a/29329118/179583) didn't?)",
